The new reasoning/tfw.py implementation adapts the bidirectional GPT-2 wrapper,
shifted-logit masked-token objective, and stochastic0.5-linear remasking logic
from src/llmtuner/tuner/mdm/model.py and trainer.py. It uses the installed
Hugging Face GPT-2 implementation, not copied GPT-2 source code.

Local changes include an isolated single-GPU optimizer loop, explicit full-state
resume contracts, global-token-count gradient accumulation, safe zero-mask
losses, leakage-filtered prepared Zebra data, independent scoring, and additional
labelled decoding controls. The monotonic decoder is a paper-informed
reconstruction, not a verbatim implementation of released author code.

This upstream repository was cited by Train for the Worst, Plan for the Best;
it is not the authors' exact released Zebra training/evaluation pipeline.
